<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shun (emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Emperor Shun, Yu Shun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shun is a legendary sage-king of early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, said to have been chosen by Emperor Yao for his virtue and filial piety and to have passed the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yu-the-great">Yu the Great</a>. Confucian tradition held him up as a model ruler. The rulers of the Zhou state of Chen claimed descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shun-emperor.jpg" alt="Shun (emperor)" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mural painting from Han dynasty · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:EmperorShun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
